BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:now and then Artist/Curator Talk: Michael Massie in Conversation w
 ith Alysa Procida
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T183000
UID:curator-talk-michael-massie-conversation-alysa-procida@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Don't miss this exclusive Artist/Curator Talk with acclaimed a
 rtist Michael Massie and guest curator Alysa Procida.\n\nnow and then Arti
 st/Curator Talk: Michael Massie in Conversation with Alysa Procida Wednesd
 ay\, October 28\, 5 p.m. to 6:30 p.m. Don't miss this exclusive Artist/Cur
 ator Talk with acclaimed artist Michael Massie and guest curator Alysa Pro
 cida . Discover the stories exhibited in now and then \, celebrating Massi
 e's remarkable career through an extraordinary collection of teapots\, pre
 viously unexhibited and new works. Together\, they will explore the joy\, 
 humour\, and experimentation that define Massie's practice\, and discuss h
 ow his exceptional craftsmanship weaves together Inuit design traditions\,
  community\, and political commentary while continually challenging expect
 ations of contemporary Inuit art. Visit Registration Page Image Credit: Mi
 chael Massie\, “pop” art in suspension \, 2025\, aluminum\, wood\, cop
 per\, string/gut. Image courtesy of Fehely Fine Arts\, photo by Renzo Fern
 andez. About the Artist Michael Massie was born in Happy Valley-Goose Bay 
 and currently resides in Kippens\, NL. His artwork reflects his mixed Inui
 t and Scottish heritage\, such as his iconic ulu teapot works. He has been
  working in sculpture\, painting\, and drawing for over thirty years and h
 as achieved artistic acclaim in Canada and internationally. His work sits 
 in collections including the Smithsonian National Museum of the American I
 ndian\, Heard Museum\, Royal Ontario Museum\, National Gallery of Canada\,
  The Rooms\, Winnipeg Art Gallery\, Montreal Museum of Fine Art\, and the 
 YVR Vancouver Airport Collection. He has been shortlisted twice for the Pr
 ix Saidye-Bronfman\, an honorary distinction for a Canadian craftsperson w
 ho demonstrates excellence in fine crafts. He was elected a member of the 
 Royal Canadian Academy of Arts in 2011 and inducted into the Order of Cana
 da in 2017. Massie received an honorary doctorate from OCAD University in 
 2024. About the Guest Curator Alysa Procida is an arts administrator\, cur
 ator\, and consultant who is passionate about connecting artists with audi
 ences across the world. She is the 2026 International Liaison for the Arct
 ic Arts Summit Secretariat\, having previously co-organized the 2022 Arcti
 c Arts Summit in Whitehorse\, YK. Previously\, she was the Executive Direc
 tor of the Inuit Art Foundation (IAF) and Publisher of the Inuit Art Quart
 erly (IAQ)\, Chair of the Magazines Canada Board of Directors\, and a ment
 or on the Inuit Futures in Arts Leadership: The Pilimmaksarniq / Pijariuqs
 arniq Project. As Publisher of the IAQ \, Alysa oversaw a full redesign of
  the magazine in conjunction with the IAF’s 30th anniversary in 2017 and
  the magazine’s first National Magazine Award in 2018. In 2019\, she was
  shortlisted for Publisher Grand Prix at the National Magazine Awards\, an
 d in 2021 the IAQ was awarded Best Arts and Literary Magazine and winner o
 f the Magazine Grand Prix. Onsite Gallery is generously supported by The D
 elaney Family We also acknowledge the support of Ontario Arts Council\, an
  agency of the Ontario Government and City of Toronto through Toronto Arts
  Council.
LOCATION:Onsite Gallery (RHD) 199 Richmond Street West 199 Richmond Street
  West
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/now-and-then-artist/curato
 r-talk-michael-massie-conversation-alysa-procida
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing Out: Art Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T235959
UID:drawing-out-art-now@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:A three-day Art festival curated by James Olley and Amy Swartz
  marking OCAD University's 150-year legacy through performance\, participa
 tion\, and expanded approaches to drawing.\n\nDrawing Out: Art Now Drawing
  Out: Art Now is a three-day Art festival curated by James Olley and Amy S
 wartz marking OCAD University's 150-year legacy through performance\, part
 icipation\, and expanded approaches to drawing. The program foregrounds co
 ntemporary art practices in which gesture\, movement\, and live action int
 ersect with mark-making. In this context\, drawing is an act of movement: 
 a way of thinking\, understanding\, and making through the body\, becoming
  both process and trace. Tuesday\, October 27 to Thursday\, October 29\, 2
 026 OCAD University\, The Great Hall\n\nSchedule Tuesday\, October 27 5:30
  PM Door Open 6:00 - 9:00 PM Drawing Disco - Draw\, dance and socialize Er
 in Finley Hors d'oeuvres\, Refreshments Above Ground Drawing Supplies incl
 uded +2 Raffle Door Prizes worth $250 each! Ticket: Wednesday\, October 28
  1:30 - 4:30 PM Drawing in 4 Parts: Folding\, Transformation\, and Process
  Natalie Waldburger | Cybèle Young | Sophie Dunkley | TooPink Free event 
 Thursday\, October 29 4:30 Door Open 5:00 - 8:00 PM Drawing to Close: Gest
 ure\, Performance\, and Transformation Francisco-Fernando Granados | James
  Knott | Pixel Heller RSVP here:
LOCATION:The Great Hall 100 McCaul St.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/drawing-out-art-now
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Conversation | Rebecca Baird and Kenny Baird with Lisa Deanne S
 mith
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T150000
UID:conversation-rebecca-baird-and-kenny-baird-lisa-deanne-smith@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging conversation and exhibition tour with 
 artists Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird\, alongside exhibition curator
  Lisa Deanne Smith\, as they explore the stories\, creative processes\, an
 d lived experiences behind Returning to Ourselves.\n\nIn Conversation | Re
 becca Baird and Kenny Baird with Lisa Deanne Smith – Saturday\, October 
 24\, 2026\, 1:00 p.m. to 3:00 p.m.\, Onsite Gallery\, 199 Richmond Street 
 West\, Toronto Join us for an engaging conversation and exhibition tour wi
 th artists Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird \, alongside exhibition cur
 ator Lisa Deanne Smith \, as they explore the stories\, creative processes
 \, and lived experiences behind Returning to Ourselves . Spanning more tha
 n four decades of artistic practice\, Returning to Ourselves showcases the
  transformative work of Rebecca and Kenny Alvin Baird through sculpture\, 
 painting\, traditional material practices\, interior design\, film art dir
 ection\, graphic design\, and public art commissions. Together\, the artis
 ts and curator will reflect on the exhibition's themes of identity\, famil
 y\, creativity\, and Cree Métis cultural continuity\, offering unique ins
 ights into the evolution of their multidisciplinary practices and the endu
 ring impact of their work. Visit Registration Page Image banner credit: Re
 becca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird \, 1991. Image courtesy of the artists.
LOCATION:Onsite Gallery (RHD) 199 Richmond Street West 199 Richmond Street
  West
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/conversation-rebecca-baird
 -and-kenny-baird-lisa-deanne-smith
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
